1
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:23,500
Only one adventure gets this wild.

2
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Jungle Cruise is a fantasy, adventure, family film
directed by Jaume Collet-Serra.

3
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:58,500
Lily Houghton enlists the aid of wisecracking skipper Frank Wolff to
take her down the Amazon in his dilapidated boat.

4
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Together, they search for an ancient tree that holds the power to heal
– a discovery that will change the future of medicine.

5
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:33,500
Frank Wolff, played by Dwayne Johnson.

6
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Dr. Lily Houghton, played by Emily Blunt.

7
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:08,500
Lope de Aguirre, played by Edgar Ramírez.

8
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:26,000
McGregor Houghton, played by Jack Whitehall.

9
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:43,500
Prince Joachim, played by Jesse Plemons.

10
00:52:55,000 --> 00:53:01,000
Nilo, played by Paul Giamatti.

11
00:58:12,500 --> 00:58:18,500
Jungle Cruise is a 2021 American fantasy adventure film
based on the Disney theme park attraction.

12
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
It stars Dwayne Johnson, Emily Blunt, Édgar Ramírez, Jack
Whitehall, Jesse Plemons, and Paul Giamatti.

13
01:08:47,500 --> 01:08:53,500
Directed by Jaume Collet-Serra from a screenplay by Glenn Ficarra, John Requa, and Michael Green, it tells the alternate history of the captain of a small riverboat who
takes a scientist and her brother through a jungle in search of the Tree of life while competing against a German expedition, and cursed conquistadors.

14
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:11,000
Plans for a feature film based on the Jungle Cruise ride began in 2004.

15
01:19:22,500 --> 01:19:28,500
The project lay dormant until 2011.

16
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
The original version fell through, and Johnson joined in 2015.

17
01:29:57,500 --> 01:30:03,500
Blunt and the rest of the cast joined in 2018 in a revamped version, with filming
taking place in Hawaii and Georgia, from May through September that year.

18
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:21,000
The score was composed by James Newton Howard.

19
01:40:32,500 --> 01:40:38,500
Following a year of post-production and a year of further delay due to the COVID-19 pandemic, Jungle Cruise premiered at Disneyland
Resort on July 24, 2021, and was released in the United States on July 30, simultaneously in theaters and digitally.

20
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:56,000
The film received mixed reviews, and was a box-office disappointment,
grossing $221 million against a budget of $200 million.

21
01:51:07,500 --> 01:51:13,500
It also made $66 million over its first 30 days on Disney+ Premier Access.

22
01:56:25,000 --> 01:56:31,000
The film explores themes of jungle, riverboat, 1910s,
amazon river, based on theme park ride.

23
02:01:42,500 --> 02:01:48,500
The tone is lighthearted.
